(4741134, 681140, 28962, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tcc:</b></div><hr/><i> Landlocked, are we...? Spur of a moment, last-minute entry?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>None of those.. I just enjoy studio work..<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tcc:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>What if you had tried to get a bit of a "panning effect" to emphasize the speed element. That way you could perhaps have increased the DOF a bit, and blurred the "wake" in the "speed stripes" instead. And gotten a "speedy" "water surface". That yellow brick at the bottom would have to go (unless of course the wheel is attached to it. Hmm). A bit of blue tack or clay instead, to get the bow to lift, perhaps? Or a bit of "spray" around the bow to hide the yellow brick? <br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oke, I could have spend a little more time on the matter.. Also turning his head and making eye-contact would have helped to make it a better shot, even while I doubt it would have done better in the contest.  <br/>Oh well.. next time better..;)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by tcc: Landlocked, are we...? Spur of a moment, last-minute entry?  None of those.. I just enjoy studio work.. Originally posted by tcc: What if you had tried to get a bit of a "panning effect" to emphasize the speed element. That way you could perhaps have increased the DOF a bit, and blurred the "wake" in the "speed stripes" instead. And gotten a "speedy" "water surface". That yellow brick at the bottom would have to go (unless of course the wheel is attached to it. Hmm). A bit of blue tack or clay instead, to get the bow to lift, perhaps? Or a bit of "spray" around the bow to hide the yellow brick?   Oke, I could have spend a little more time on the matter.. Also turning his head and making eye-contact would have helped to make it a better shot, even while I doubt it would have done better in the contest.  Oh well.. next time better..;)', '2008-06-02 09:18:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741139, 681140, 28962, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and remarks.. !</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and remarks.. !', '2008-06-02 09:18:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741149, 681091, 52549, '<td valign="top">I loved this image on first sight. The sepia toning fits perfectly and I especially like the rowing boat tethered to the ship. GREAT work, Tim.</td>', 'I loved this image on first sight. The sepia toning fits perfectly and I especially like the rowing boat tethered to the ship. GREAT work, Tim.', '2008-06-02 09:21:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741151, 681812, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657243" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg"/></a> what an interesting, and well executed image.  will it sound self-serving to say i saw what you did almost immediately?  however, what you did was superb.  the illusions created by the pool deck above water put the boat in a world of its own, a tiny little globe of water.  o, and those colours...  yes. o yes.</td>', ' what an interesting, and well executed image.  will it sound self-serving to say i saw what you did almost immediately?  however, what you did was superb.  the illusions created by the pool deck above water put the boat in a world of its own, a tiny little globe of water.  o, and those colours...  yes. o yes.', '2008-06-02 09:21:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741156, 681410, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657242" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg"/></a> ooo, lovely colours, tones, colours, o, and those colours...  this is another that grabs you in the guts.  the left side, so crisp and clean, the right a chaos of shadows and motion.  the anarchy threatening to overtake the order.  and those blues...mmmmm.....</td>', ' ooo, lovely colours, tones, colours, o, and those colours...  this is another that grabs you in the guts.  the left side, so crisp and clean, the right a chaos of shadows and motion.  the anarchy threatening to overtake the order.  and those blues...mmmmm.....', '2008-06-02 09:22:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741160, 681091, 67152, '<td valign="top">tim - nice job kicking this one up a notch in processing.</td>', 'tim - nice job kicking this one up a notch in processing.', '2008-06-02 09:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741162, 681990, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657241" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg"/></a> two x-prizes in a row.  cool.  this, like the camera portrait, has a wonderful feeling of disturbed light and dark.  the textures, the colours, the blur, all work together extremely well.  this piece creates an emotional reaction, not just on an aesthetic level, but a visceral level as well.  an image not to analyse but to embrace and experience.  well done indeed.</td>', ' two x-prizes in a row.  cool.  this, like the camera portrait, has a wonderful feeling of disturbed light and dark.  the textures, the colours, the blur, all work together extremely well.  this piece creates an emotional reaction, not just on an aesthetic level, but a visceral level as well.  an image not to analyse but to embrace and experience.  well done indeed.', '2008-06-02 09:23:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741168, 681812, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very cool...  I did not guess this was an underwater shot!  So clever!</td>', 'Very cool...  I did not guess this was an underwater shot!  So clever!', '2008-06-02 09:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4741172, 681990, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xianart:</b></div><hr/><i> this piece creates an emotional reaction, not just on an aesthetic level, but a visceral level as well.  an image not to analyse but to embrace and experience.  well done indeed. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, what she said. :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-02 08:27:36.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by xianart: this piece creates an emotional reaction, not just on an aesthetic level, but a visceral level as well.  an image not to analyse but to embrace and experience.  well done indeed.  Yes, what she said. :-)', '2008-06-02 09:27:27.000000', '2008-06-02 09:27:36.000000', 0),
(4741176, 682196, 23484, '<td valign="top">First of all, I think the title is magnificent! I didn''t vote in this challenge so this is my first time seeing it. I think the shot is great and I love the way the wake is blown out like that. I also like the Rule-of-thirds layered look. Just goes to show how SHALLOW this place can be (pun intended).</td>', 'First of all, I think the title is magnificent! I didn''t vote in this challenge so this is my first time seeing it. I think the shot is great and I love the way the wake is blown out like that. I also like the Rule-of-thirds layered look. Just goes to show how SHALLOW this place can be (pun intended).', '2008-06-02 09:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
