(4749043, 681406, 81030, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jaker:</b></div><hr/><i> Read your comments up there, and I definitely would have lied and said that was the name of the boat.  Who would have known?  I''m also curious if you can give the translations for BEGINNERS LUCK!  Or how about, "Let''s see you do that again THIS week!" :-)<br/> <br/>Seriously though, one of my top three for this challenge, and already making a home in my favorites.  Excellent work! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>About the "beginners luck"  I am a beginner but about the luck, we just have to wait and see.  :)  <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment u all again. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Jaker: Read your comments up there, and I definitely would have lied and said that was the name of the boat.  Who would have known?  I''m also curious if you can give the translations for BEGINNERS LUCK!  Or how about, "Let''s see you do that again THIS week!" :-) Seriously though, one of my top three for this challenge, and already making a home in my favorites.  Excellent work!   About the "beginners luck"  I am a beginner but about the luck, we just have to wait and see.  :)   Thanks for the comment u all again.  ', '2008-06-04 15:10:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4749045, 681967, 4517, '<td valign="top">Terrific ir photo Irene. Congrats on another well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Terrific ir photo Irene. Congrats on another well deserved ribbon.', '2008-06-04 15:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4749624, 681406, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club....?<br/> <br/>Not a lot to say about this shot. There''s not really any way to improve it in any event. As pointed out, a tiny bit of movement in the bow made some of it a little less sharp but its neglible. The long shutter speed gave the water a extremely smooth appearance which I think is part of what makes this shot. The reflection is also terrific. Composition is bang on.  I''d like to give the 5 people who only gave this a a 4 or 5 a slap in the head. Great entry. Congrats on the blue!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club....? Not a lot to say about this shot. There''s not really any way to improve it in any event. As pointed out, a tiny bit of movement in the bow made some of it a little less sharp but its neglible. The long shutter speed gave the water a extremely smooth appearance which I think is part of what makes this shot. The reflection is also terrific. Composition is bang on.  I''d like to give the 5 people who only gave this a a 4 or 5 a slap in the head. Great entry. Congrats on the blue!', '2008-06-04 19:18:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4749675, 682098, 68035, '<td valign="top">Hey Karen, you already got my view on this shot but I just wanted to add by congrats on the top 10 finish!!!!  Great image and thoroughly deserved it</td>', 'Hey Karen, you already got my view on this shot but I just wanted to add by congrats on the top 10 finish!!!!  Great image and thoroughly deserved it', '2008-06-04 19:38:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4749885, 681410, 42013, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, ghostlike, full of possibilities. Nice work!</td>', 'Beautiful, ghostlike, full of possibilities. Nice work!', '2008-06-04 21:21:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4751234, 682075, 48910, '<td valign="top">This is so absolutely gorgeous!</td>', 'This is so absolutely gorgeous!', '2008-06-05 10:03:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4752919, 682098, 39057, '<td valign="top">You are very lucky to live near these types of scenes! <br/>Good Job.</td>', 'You are very lucky to live near these types of scenes! Good Job.', '2008-06-05 22:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753062, 682115, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club!<br/> <br/>Interesting subject and a great find for this challenge. The colors are what I find really appealing in this shot. Exposure is fairly well handled however the sky is a little dark and as mentioned the masking did strange things to the clouds.  I think the composition could be improved perhaps by shooting from more of an oblique. It would also be nice to see water in the shot (if that was possible). <br/> <br/>Overall a good image</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club! Interesting subject and a great find for this challenge. The colors are what I find really appealing in this shot. Exposure is fairly well handled however the sky is a little dark and as mentioned the masking did strange things to the clouds.  I think the composition could be improved perhaps by shooting from more of an oblique. It would also be nice to see water in the shot (if that was possible).  Overall a good image', '2008-06-05 23:54:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753219, 681975, 68504, '<td valign="top">Very pleasing image.</td>', 'Very pleasing image.', '2008-06-06 02:38:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753228, 682125, 68504, '<td valign="top">Delightful.  Everything well done.  (I may know some other cows where she comes from).</td>', 'Delightful.  Everything well done.  (I may know some other cows where she comes from).', '2008-06-06 02:49:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753229, 681140, 68504, '<td valign="top">My hat is off to anyone who can capture a big white stern spray.</td>', 'My hat is off to anyone who can capture a big white stern spray.', '2008-06-06 02:51:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753232, 681953, 68504, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity in this; the water is sumptuous.</td>', 'I like the simplicity in this; the water is sumptuous.', '2008-06-06 02:55:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753234, 681689, 68504, '<td valign="top">Most engaging!</td>', 'Most engaging!', '2008-06-06 02:57:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753240, 682195, 68504, '<td valign="top">Those reflections! (Really miss the tip of the boat though. Why one''s processing program crashes so close to the deadlines makes me very suspicious of the electronic world!)</td>', 'Those reflections! (Really miss the tip of the boat though. Why one''s processing program crashes so close to the deadlines makes me very suspicious of the electronic world!)', '2008-06-06 03:01:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753251, 681872, 68504, '<td valign="top">Clearly this is a daytime outing, the boat being paper and all, so I very impressed it has a built in lamp cause you never know.  A wonderful sense of just happening in this.</td>', 'Clearly this is a daytime outing, the boat being paper and all, so I very impressed it has a built in lamp cause you never know.  A wonderful sense of just happening in this.', '2008-06-06 03:05:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753267, 681994, 68504, '<td valign="top">This is quite charming.  Makes me think of The Wind in The Willows.</td>', 'This is quite charming.  Makes me think of The Wind in The Willows.', '2008-06-06 03:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753280, 681986, 68504, '<td valign="top">Yes, two very impressive cruisers.</td>', 'Yes, two very impressive cruisers.', '2008-06-06 03:18:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753287, 681046, 68504, '<td valign="top">Quite taken with this composition, though I wish it were straightened, and that we could see the top of the mast on this wonderful orange-hulled boat which sets off or is set off by the greyish toned shoreline buildings. (Doesn''t say snapshot to me).</td>', 'Quite taken with this composition, though I wish it were straightened, and that we could see the top of the mast on this wonderful orange-hulled boat which sets off or is set off by the greyish toned shoreline buildings. (Doesn''t say snapshot to me).', '2008-06-06 03:23:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753544, 681062, 53147, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club -<br/> <br/>From a quick browse through the comments you recieved I see that I will probably sound like a broken record on certain aspects. <br/> <br/>You met the challenge for sure. There is a recognizable boat in the shot. But there are some issues here that definitely kept you from bringing in the higher votes from the (very picky) DPC crowd. Night shots of moving targets are tough. You did well using your high ISO and longer than usual shutter speed for (I am assuming) a handheld shot. I am surprised you didnt get more motion blur on your subject. But it still isnt as sharp as most DPC''ers are looking for. <br/> <br/>Your tilted horizon is a big issue for most dpcers as well. They like either a straight horizon or an obviously intended tilt. This shot doesnt feel tilt intended. Straightening that up I think would have given you several tenths onto your score.<br/> <br/>Your background while very cool (and I would keep that in mind for future challenges) competes with your boat. My eye is drawn more to the city scape and the boat starts to blend in with the city lights.<br/> <br/>That all said - I really like the variety of lights and colors you have here. The NN did pretty good taking care of most of your noise issues. <br/> <br/>Looking at your vote curve you realize tat it could be much worse. 5.1 average isnt great but you didnt really have alot of people who hated this shot. But in the end you didnt strike a chord either way. <br/> <br/>I see you have been here just since March. Welcome! I hope you are finding your time spent here well worth it. There is a ton of info on this site that is worth gold. Pay attention to what people are doing and how they do it and keep on entering. Your scores will continue to go up.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club - From a quick browse through the comments you recieved I see that I will probably sound like a broken record on certain aspects.  You met the challenge for sure. There is a recognizable boat in the shot. But there are some issues here that definitely kept you from bringing in the higher votes from the (very picky) DPC crowd. Night shots of moving targets are tough. You did well using your high ISO and longer than usual shutter speed for (I am assuming) a handheld shot. I am surprised you didnt get more motion blur on your subject. But it still isnt as sharp as most DPC''ers are looking for.  Your tilted horizon is a big issue for most dpcers as well. They like either a straight horizon or an obviously intended tilt. This shot doesnt feel tilt intended. Straightening that up I think would have given you several tenths onto your score. Your background while very cool (and I would keep that in mind for future challenges) competes with your boat. My eye is drawn more to the city scape and the boat starts to blend in with the city lights. That all said - I really like the variety of lights and colors you have here. The NN did pretty good taking care of most of your noise issues.  Looking at your vote curve you realize tat it could be much worse. 5.1 average isnt great but you didnt really have alot of people who hated this shot. But in the end you didnt strike a chord either way.  I see you have been here just since March. Welcome! I hope you are finding your time spent here well worth it. There is a ton of info on this site that is worth gold. Pay attention to what people are doing and how they do it and keep on entering. Your scores will continue to go up. Tim', '2008-06-06 08:08:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753547, 682026, 53147, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club - <br/> <br/>Solid shot here. Easily meets the challenge. The long exposure works great, excellent light, great detail and a wonderful smooth feel to the image. If this were my shot I may have dodged the boats a bit to make them stand out a bit more prominently but as is its still a lovely scene. <br/> <br/>Not much else to add here. A very nice shot with a very good score attached to it. Well done.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club -  Solid shot here. Easily meets the challenge. The long exposure works great, excellent light, great detail and a wonderful smooth feel to the image. If this were my shot I may have dodged the boats a bit to make them stand out a bit more prominently but as is its still a lovely scene.  Not much else to add here. A very nice shot with a very good score attached to it. Well done. Tim', '2008-06-06 08:11:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753557, 681103, 53147, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club - <br/> <br/>Well you almost nailed the brown. I wont make this long as it looks like I will just be repeating most of what your other comments state.<br/> <br/>You met the challenge for sure, but the technical issues really over power that. The blurry issue is just a really strong problem. Odds are this was handheld with a long shutter speed (long for hand held) and that ends up being all I think about when looking at the shot. <br/> <br/>I do think you have a cool "model" here though. A wide angle lens (or standing further back) to allow the whole boat to be in the shot, and shooting on a tripod to allow a sharper shot would have served you much better here.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club -  Well you almost nailed the brown. I wont make this long as it looks like I will just be repeating most of what your other comments state. You met the challenge for sure, but the technical issues really over power that. The blurry issue is just a really strong problem. Odds are this was handheld with a long shutter speed (long for hand held) and that ends up being all I think about when looking at the shot.  I do think you have a cool "model" here though. A wide angle lens (or standing further back) to allow the whole boat to be in the shot, and shooting on a tripod to allow a sharper shot would have served you much better here. Tim', '2008-06-06 08:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4753573, 681819, 53147, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club - <br/> <br/>Just read your description - "best of a bad bunch". LOL - We have all been there for sure. Though I don''t think this is as bad as the score you recieved.<br/> <br/>You easily met the challenge. The HDR treatment may be a tad heavy on this shot. What I tend to do when I do editing similar to HDR is bump up the blacks a bit afterwards. In this shot everything comes off as almost too pastelly (is that a word). I think if the blacks were a bit more black the image would have popped a bit more.<br/> <br/>Really not a horrible shot - just one that didnt reson te with the DPC crowd. We really are a finnicky bunch arent we.<br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club -  Just read your description - "best of a bad bunch". LOL - We have all been there for sure. Though I don''t think this is as bad as the score you recieved. You easily met the challenge. The HDR treatment may be a tad heavy on this shot. What I tend to do when I do editing similar to HDR is bump up the blacks a bit afterwards. In this shot everything comes off as almost too pastelly (is that a word). I think if the blacks were a bit more black the image would have popped a bit more. Really not a horrible shot - just one that didnt reson te with the DPC crowd. We really are a finnicky bunch arent we. Tim', '2008-06-06 08:20:26.000000', NULL, 0),
