(5091330, 682073, 90495, '<td valign="top">I like HDR. No matter what anyone says about it. Hope the negative comments don''t dissuade you in doing more. I think the one''s who don''t like it simply cannot produce it to this quality. <br/> <br/>I wonder what people said way back when Daguerre was first producing plates (Daguerreotypes)?</td>', 'I like HDR. No matter what anyone says about it. Hope the negative comments don''t dissuade you in doing more. I think the one''s who don''t like it simply cannot produce it to this quality.  I wonder what people said way back when Daguerre was first producing plates (Daguerreotypes)?', '2008-11-30 12:31:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5445490, 682190, 90495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tootsweet:</b></div><hr/><i> Too dark for my tastes.  Sometimes the beauty of a storm cloud is more impressive when left alone.  I almost get the feeling that you took a picture on a nice day and processed it to this point.  The boats are completely obscured and not really an element due to the darkness of the clouds and the deck in the foreground. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not quite.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-28 23:55:13.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tootsweet: Too dark for my tastes.  Sometimes the beauty of a storm cloud is more impressive when left alone.  I almost get the feeling that you took a picture on a nice day and processed it to this point.  The boats are completely obscured and not really an element due to the darkness of the clouds and the deck in the foreground.   Not quite.', '2009-04-20 14:32:15.000000', '2009-04-29 00:55:13.000000', 0),
